[18.595499, "o", "You are Codex, taking over a coding task through Baton.\r\nThe previous agent paused (usually because its usage limit is close). Its handoff is below; the same file is HANDOFF.md at the repo root.\r\n\r\nRules:\r\n1. First reply with ONE line: \"Continuing: <goal in a few words>. Next: <next step>.\" Then start working.\r\n2. Do not retry anything listed under \"Rejected\". Respect \"Decisions\".\r\n3. The handoff is a lossy summary — if something is unclear, check git log/diff before redoing work.\r\n4. When you stop, update HANDOFF.md (Done / Next / Open questions) so the next agent can continue.\r\n\r\n----- HANDOFF.md -----\r\n---\r\nbaton_version: 0.1.0\r\nfrom: claude\r\nto: codex\r\ncreated_at: 2026-10-31T11:23:51.589Z\r\nupdated_at: 2026-10-31T11:24:00.599Z\r\nquota_at: unknown\r\nquota_at_5h: unknown\r\nquota_at_7d: unknown\r\ntriggered_by: manual\r\nstatus: manual\r\n---\r\n\r\n# HANDOFF\r\n\r\n> Written by Baton. Agents: read this first, restate the Goal and the next step in one line, then continue.\r\n> Structured handoff is lossy — if something is unclear, check git history before redoing work.\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\n- _(to fill)_\r\n\r\n## Done\r\n- _(to fill)_\r\n\r\n## Decisions\r\n"]
